# What Prettier is not allowed to touch. Reasoning in DECISIONS.md D-142.
#
# The rule: Prettier formats hand-written code in `web/`. It does not format prose, generated
# files, or anything vendored from upstream. Each block below is one of those three.

# ── Build output and caches ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
.next/
out/
build/
node_modules/
.frozen/
.shots/
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# ── Generated by a tool that will regenerate them ─────────────────────────────
# `drizzle-kit generate` rewrites meta/*.json from its own serializer. Formatting them means
# the next `npm run db:generate` reverts the formatting, so `--check` fails on a clean tree
# through no fault of anyone's. The .sql files are here for the same reason; Prettier has no
# SQL parser anyway, so they are only listed to make the intent explicit.
drizzle/
package-lock.json
# `npm run tokens` rewrites src/app/tokens.css from its own serializer, and `tokens:check`
# compares the two byte for byte. Formatting it means the next generate reverts the formatting
# and the staleness check fails on a clean tree — the same trap as drizzle/ above.
src/app/tokens.css
# Same arrangement for src/app/scale.css: `npm run scale` rewrites it and `scale:check`
# compares byte for byte (V4 §1.5–§1.9, D-199).
src/app/scale.css

# ── Formerly vendored from the shadcn registry ────────────────────────────────
# Nothing is excluded here any more, and that is V4 §1.10 (D-200, Q473).
#
# This block used to exclude `src/components/ui/*.tsx` because those files arrived from the
# registry with 500–1200 character class strings on one line, and reformatting them would make
# every future `shadcn add` produce a diff against our formatting instead of a clean re-vendor.
# That argument depended on the directory still being upstream's. It is not: ten unused files
# were deleted and the nine that remain were hand-reworked at the V4 tokens, so a future
# `shadcn add` would overwrite our work rather than merge with it. They are ours now, and
# Prettier owns them like everything else in `src/`.
#
# The block also carried `!src/components/ui/form.tsx`, a negation protecting a file that has
# never existed in this repo or its history — see D-200. Removed with it.

# ── Prose ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Markdown here is hand-wrapped documentation, not code. Prettier's default
# `proseWrap: "preserve"` leaves paragraphs alone but still rewrites tables and lists — that
# is 133KB of pure churn in DECISIONS.md alone, in the file most often read to answer "why
# is this like this".
#
# AGENTS.md is the concrete case: `next dev` rewrites its <!-- BEGIN:nextjs-agent-rules -->
# block on every run. If Prettier reformats that block, every `next dev` produces an
# uncommitted change and the two tools fight forever.
#
# The vault at ../context/ is outside this directory and so out of scope already, but it is
# worth stating that it must stay that way: those files are parsed by scripts/build_indexes.py
# and their formatting is load-bearing.
*.md

# ── Static assets ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
public/
